export const body = "<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>TOPIC INTRODUCTION</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>SHAPE FUNDAMENTALS</strong></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\n<p>The primary goal of a language is communication. In literature, people string words together to convey their thoughts and ideas. In visual art, shapes are the words, and the ways artists construct them can similarly send a message to viewers.</p>\n<p>In this document, we will study the fundamental shapes and their usage in different areas. Our goal is to help you create artworks that speak for themselves.</p>\n<p>But first, let’s watch a short film!<strong><br></strong></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0daa2460bee92216662e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0daa2460bee92216662e.webp\" width=\"333\" height=\"450\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Next Door</strong></p>\n<p>He has worked on <em>Toy Story</em>, <em>Monster, Inc</em>., <em>WALL-E</em>, and <em>Inside Out</em>. When you look into his portfolio, you can immediately notice his unique approach to character design. He relishes geometry.</p>\n<p><em>Next Door</em>, a traditional hand-drawn animated short he submitted to his university, is a great showcase of shape language. It is a story told just by squares, circles, and triangles.</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A disparate world</strong></p>\n<p>The very first image we see of <em>Next Door</em> is a circle breaking apart, signifying the division in the world and the people in it.</p>\n<p>The film then eases us into the story via a simple composition: a box and sphere separated by a triangular road. From this one frame, the director establishes the theme both physically and figuratively.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/200c26547d4c150efcb3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/200c26547d4c150efcb3.webp\" width=\"767\" height=\"883\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A grumpy square</strong></p>\n<p>Our main character is a middle-aged man who fixates his life on rules. We can tell that by the way he acts based on his watch—everything has to be on time. Not only is his home a big block, every object in the interior is either a square or a rectangle.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/121b4b321bf960681f0d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/121b4b321bf960681f0d.webp\" width=\"579\" height=\"883\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A cheerful circle</strong></p>\n<p>Then, there is a little girl living next to him, who is full of energy and joy. She lets her imagination run wild, and her imaginations are made of circles.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/076aa05973c3dae4802b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/076aa05973c3dae4802b.webp\" width=\"1089\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A stark contrast</strong></p>\n<p>As the noises she makes get to the grumpy man, he looks out of the windowpane, showing us the emotional and visual contrast between them. Moments later, we see them boxed in frames: he is in a square, she in an oval.</p>\n<p>Even though they are both “trapped”, they emote differently: he is trapped in annoyance, she in excitement.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3f2cd81194777a1e98c8.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3f2cd81194777a1e98c8.webp\" width=\"396\" height=\"302\" style=\"--source-width:282px\" alt=\"Illustration 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d6d1475ac7694b2b74f4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d6d1475ac7694b2b74f4.webp\" width=\"547\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A transition</strong></p>\n<p>But once he hears the harmonica sounds coming from the little girl, he recalls his younger days—the times when he was still enjoying his life. He realizes that there is still fun to be had.</p>\n<p>That sudden realization puts a smile on his face, turning it into rounder shapes with curvier lines.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d061c692431a7f6ba8eb.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d061c692431a7f6ba8eb.webp\" width=\"369\" height=\"278\" style=\"--source-width:282px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/52cfac7ec990ea0de716.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/52cfac7ec990ea0de716.webp\" width=\"954\" height=\"709\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 8\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A full circle</strong></p>\n<p>The film ends with two shapes from a distance connecting and forming one full circle,. It signifies the reconnection of a community, contrasting the fragmentation of the beginning.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c9f93248576e332fb803.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c9f93248576e332fb803.webp\" width=\"771\" height=\"883\" style=\"--source-width:263px\" alt=\"Illustration 9\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<h2>Chapter 01: Shape Basics</h2>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>TABLE OF CONTENT</strong></p><p><strong>Chapter 01: Shape Basics </strong></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Primary shapes</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Circle</li><li>Square</li><li>Triangle</li><li>Summary</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Be flexible not literal</li></ul></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>CONTENT</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\n<p>The design principles in Next Door permeate throughout many animated films. They still create characters and worlds from simple shapes. They let different shapes contrast and elevate each other. And they transform shapes to denote thematic changes.</p>\n<p>In this document, we will focus on the primary shapes: circles, squares, and triangles.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/16ef45a742c30c10d7cc.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/16ef45a742c30c10d7cc.webp\" width=\"947\" height=\"533\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 10\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1423e2c08c154b0d8ba7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1423e2c08c154b0d8ba7.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"477\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 11\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>Anton Ego's triangular face turns into a circle.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Primary shapes</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Circle</strong></p>\n<p>Circles and ovals evoke wholeness and protection. Using these shapes on an object or a character will make them more approachable. Besides, circles are also organic and natural shapes.</p>\n<p>However, you shouldn’t use perfectly circular and oval shapes. You can mix and alter the shapes to improve the design.</p>\n<p><strong>TIP</strong>: Round out the edges and add curves to your design instead of focusing on the whole shape.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/54f67b352f023f9f1144.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/54f67b352f023f9f1144.webp\" width=\"834\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 12\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Square</strong></p>\n<p>Squares (or rectangles) feel sturdy and strong, but also artificial and manufactured. While we can see round and point shapes in nature, we can’t find perfectly square shapes in it.</p>\n<p>You shouldn’t leave perfectly square edges and corners in your design unless it is a manufactured object. Try to round or taper them a bit, especially for organic objects.</p>\n<p><strong>TIP</strong>: you can use square shapes on the jaw, shoulders, and hands of a character to make them feel strong and a bit difficult to move.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/6783a795a10b60574915.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/6783a795a10b60574915.webp\" width=\"774\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 13\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Triangle</strong></p>\n<p>Triangles are sharp, thus often feel dangerous. The size and length of a triangle determine how menacing a character is (or how unapproachable an object is).</p>\n<p>Since the lines will converge at some points, you can use it to guide the viewer’s eyes.</p>\n<p><strong>TIP</strong>: Using too many points on one design can make it feel confusing. So unless it is meant to be confusing, you should try to avoid that.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/bde8045cc9ff45e12011.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/bde8045cc9ff45e12011.webp\" width=\"898\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 14\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Summary</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Circle</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Friendly</li><li>Protective</li><li>Enclosed</li><li>Spinning</li><li>Eternal</li><li>Etc.</li></ul></td><td><p><strong>Triangle</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Dangerous</li><li>Directional</li><li>Dynamic (due to diagonal lines)</li><li>Stable when pointing upward</li><li>Unstable when pointing downward</li><li>Etc.</li></ul></td><td><p><strong>Rectangle</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Strong</li><li>Stable</li><li>Artificial</li><li>Balanced</li><li>Etc.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4fe08697dbb905934ce5.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4fe08697dbb905934ce5.webp\" width=\"720\" height=\"480\" style=\"--source-width:87px\" alt=\"Illustration 15\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2aec40612ca5526598a5.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2aec40612ca5526598a5.webp\" width=\"720\" height=\"480\" style=\"--source-width:87px\" alt=\"Illustration 16\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/82c00e92455165468a39.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/82c00e92455165468a39.webp\" width=\"720\" height=\"480\" style=\"--source-width:87px\" alt=\"Illustration 17\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXTRA</strong>—So, what about organic shapes?</p>\n<p>Organic shapes mostly exist in nature (vegetation). They represent softness, flexibility and fluidity. They often combine <strong>C-curves</strong>, <strong>S-curves</strong>, and <strong>straight lines</strong>.</p>\n<p>Humans can still create organic shapes, but those products are luxury since they are more difficult to manufacture.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7354141a44a6c9f142e2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7354141a44a6c9f142e2.webp\" width=\"577\" height=\"292\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 18\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3806b6c28cda366c8279.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3806b6c28cda366c8279.webp\" width=\"886\" height=\"897\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 19\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Be flexible not literal</strong></p>\n<p>Now that we have covered the basics, we should understand that art is not rigid. Rarely do we create anything that is perfectly geometric. What we often do is drawing shapes that evoke the feeling of a triangle, a circle, or a square.</p>\n<p>As you can see in this picture <strong>the pointy roof counteracts the hard edges</strong> of the surrounding rock, thus creating a contrast in shapes. Even when we remove colors and break the composition, this house still stand out thanks to that contrast.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9df12a407d90bd5b0876.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9df12a407d90bd5b0876.webp\" width=\"907\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 20\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p>In these illustrations of the Lord of the Rings trilogy, the artist used round shapes for Shire, rectangle shapes for Minas Tirith, and triangular shapes for Mount Doom.  Even when we remove the colors, these shapes still can communicate the mood and tone.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/363692785b970dd82bb2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/363692785b970dd82bb2.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"418\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 21\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<h2>Chapter 02: Character Design</h2>\n\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>TABLE OF CONTENT</strong></p><p><strong>Chapter 02: Character Design </strong></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Circle</li><li>Rectangle</li><li>Triangle</li><li>Form follows function</li><li>EXTRA</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Form doesn’t follow function</li><li>Shape contrast</li><li>Beyond geometry</li></ul></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>CONTENT</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\n<p>As we learn from the short film Next Door, shapes can dictate the way we perceive a character. Based on the body frame, we can tell whether a character is friendly, strong, or dangerous.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/85b5616bd8bfaa8b88a9.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/85b5616bd8bfaa8b88a9.webp\" width=\"844\" height=\"938\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 23\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/194283a24ef9d3bf7c07.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/194283a24ef9d3bf7c07.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"455\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 24\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circle</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Circular characters are cute, friendly, and soft.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/539596ec1604b7b8c721.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/539596ec1604b7b8c721.webp\" width=\"660\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 25\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4eb52b7cc3a1497453a1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4eb52b7cc3a1497453a1.webp\" width=\"1148\" height=\"582\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 26\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p>Even though Mike Wazowski is a monster, he doesn’t look scary at all. Because of that, his peers make of him. But at the end of the Monster Inc., he becomes a comedian thanks to his approachable appearance.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a47fbff10a2c0022cbcd.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a47fbff10a2c0022cbcd.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"314\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 27\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Both the kid and the long-neck dinosaur in The Good Dinosaur have very round designs compared to other creatures.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/72d5ebc1509684023d0c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/72d5ebc1509684023d0c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"844\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 28\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Saphira in Eragon and Toothless in How To Train Your Dragon both have round body parts.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/067e25a6deecb725bab2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/067e25a6deecb725bab2.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"296\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 29\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>And of course, fairy-tale princesses have round shape language.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/862f4280798fb2d08e2a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/862f4280798fb2d08e2a.webp\" width=\"613\" height=\"897\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 30\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2d88e901097987ab473b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2d88e901097987ab473b.webp\" width=\"587\" height=\"368\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 31\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The good characters in Ori and the Will of the Wisps have round body shapes, which make them look soft and friendly.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2432105c884b7addbc5c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2432105c884b7addbc5c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"340\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 32\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/98fbbbfa8da5875c28ee.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/98fbbbfa8da5875c28ee.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"491\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 33\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3efc9f6652bb7d433e66.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3efc9f6652bb7d433e66.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"652\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 34\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0c643cc9698987128114.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0c643cc9698987128114.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"550\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 35\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3746e8f2eab1766f6602.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3746e8f2eab1766f6602.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"565\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 36\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Rectangle</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Block shapes make a character feel strong and independent, but also quite stubborn (does not like to change).</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/545f05e8855b076aa865.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/545f05e8855b076aa865.webp\" width=\"660\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 37\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/cb968608bc23d4def121.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/cb968608bc23d4def121.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"383\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 38\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f9a45882b2d5507c7778.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f9a45882b2d5507c7778.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"380\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 39\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong></p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/441f22f52c72e8576eb2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/441f22f52c72e8576eb2.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"504\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 40\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong></p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/496929ba72eeb63c3c58.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/496929ba72eeb63c3c58.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"459\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 41\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Triangle</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Triangles can make a character look evil, unstable and dangerous.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/6ecfbbe79422a47bc163.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/6ecfbbe79422a47bc163.webp\" width=\"660\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 42\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0918d66b52f00213cb52.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0918d66b52f00213cb52.webp\" width=\"1129\" height=\"520\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 43\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p>Joker is a downward triangle: he is crazy, unstable and evil.</p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/38472fee00161a303236.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/38472fee00161a303236.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"305\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 44\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Pyramid head is an iconic monster in the Silent Hill series. It is often the scariest part of the games.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/bf9f6d66b97b0482c94b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/bf9f6d66b97b0482c94b.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"323\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 45\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>The slim, triangular forms of these monsters suggest that they are fast and aggressive.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/06b66d9bfe4f90e1839e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/06b66d9bfe4f90e1839e.webp\" width=\"845\" height=\"505\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 46\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/05f82d32691cc39ad271.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/05f82d32691cc39ad271.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"238\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 47\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Despite the many rectangular elements in the body, this design still feels unfriendly due to the spiky helmet.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/297247eec3474d4e8027.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/297247eec3474d4e8027.webp\" width=\"1045\" height=\"912\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 48\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The Nazgul in Lord of the Rings universe are often depicted with spiky armor.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c48abce8fee872004993.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c48abce8fee872004993.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"334\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 49\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/618664d0ce483584b332.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/618664d0ce483584b332.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"458\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 50\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/59d0e9750d1b20342446.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/59d0e9750d1b20342446.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"462\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 51\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Form follows function</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>We can combine different shapes to convey different traits of a character. For example, Samus in the Metroid series has all three primary shapes in her design; she is friendly, strong and fast.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c7f1292ad4a82c373778.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c7f1292ad4a82c373778.webp\" width=\"422\" height=\"600\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 52\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f2a225b62637e0094bfa.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f2a225b62637e0094bfa.webp\" width=\"515\" height=\"351\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 53\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Even though Mario and Sonic both have very rounded shape language (to evoke friendliness), Sonic has some spiky shapes to suggest his super speed similar to Dash in The Incredible.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4d6725938288a4b804f1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4d6725938288a4b804f1.webp\" width=\"950\" height=\"877\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 54\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>In Batman: The Animated Series, Batman was designed with rectangles and triangles: he had a rectangular body and face, with triangular elements only on his suit. But in the The Batman series, his design was mainly triangles.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/06a4dc92fb14d12be1fa.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/06a4dc92fb14d12be1fa.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"324\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 55\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Hellboy is usually a rectangle: he is strong and resilient. But once his horns fully come out, his strength is enhanced at the cost of his consciousness.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a1ae7732b3e3a9293b0c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a1ae7732b3e3a9293b0c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"819\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 56\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Even though Hollow Knight and Hornet has a relatively similar fighting style, Hornet is way more nimble. Thus, her design is curvier and pointier to reflect that difference.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d0a926f16220c9e920cb.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d0a926f16220c9e920cb.webp\" width=\"600\" height=\"338\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 57\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ed95da4f23a540a82ff6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ed95da4f23a540a82ff6.webp\" width=\"772\" height=\"887\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 58\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>From left to right we have: Revali, Mipha, and Daruk from Breath of the Wild.</p>\n<ul><li>Revali gives Link the ability to jump extremely high</li><li>Mipha gives Link the ability to resurrect himself</li><li>Daruk gives Link the ability to shield himself</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/96e8f2c372adafb2dfad.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/96e8f2c372adafb2dfad.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"304\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 59\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>These are some agents from Valorant. From left to right we have: Cypher, Brimstone, and Sage.</p>\n<ul><li>Cypher is a scout operating in shadow.</li><li>Brimstone is a frontline heavy hitter.</li><li>Sage is a backline medic.</li></ul></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/806bcbc76408f2d454ae.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/806bcbc76408f2d454ae.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"867\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 60\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXTRA</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Form doesn’t follow function</strong></p>\n<p>You can always bend the rule. Just like real life, round shapes can be harmful, and sharp shapes are not always dangerous.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/befe66c103f0baaa804e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/befe66c103f0baaa804e.webp\" width=\"483\" height=\"273\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 61\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c49c2c9ca5e42e00dfce.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c49c2c9ca5e42e00dfce.webp\" width=\"938\" height=\"941\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 62\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>This is Paolumu in Monster Hunter: World. Do not let its fluffy appearance deceive you. This is a predator.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ce16c4cdb1a5d2f15528.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ce16c4cdb1a5d2f15528.webp\" width=\"847\" height=\"478\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 63\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/bbcf5008a5421a1d50e1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/bbcf5008a5421a1d50e1.webp\" width=\"570\" height=\"570\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 64\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>AUTO and GLaDoS, the villains of Wall-E and Portal respectively, both have rounded designs. But the red eyeball could give away AUTO’s villainous nature.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/365a8355984194a041b2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/365a8355984194a041b2.webp\" width=\"363\" height=\"242\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 65\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ef5cfa6f5cf28943138b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ef5cfa6f5cf28943138b.webp\" width=\"459\" height=\"570\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 66\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Shape contrast</strong></p>\n<p>Having characters with different shapes together can increase the visual interest in storytelling. Next door has a rectangular old man and a circular little girl; Up similarly has a rectangular old mand with many circular characters.</p>\n<p>In Wall-E, Eve stands out because she is the only clean, oval being in a weathered, square world.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/cca7909d8ba08d108566.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/cca7909d8ba08d108566.webp\" width=\"862\" height=\"940\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 67\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/73bd0cc8124d55215892.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/73bd0cc8124d55215892.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"317\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 68\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>An example from the Kungfu Panda trilogy.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ca86ae944a42a4590b14.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ca86ae944a42a4590b14.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"324\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 69\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Generally, animation is the perfect playground for shapes.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a6006d003c02331edc3a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a6006d003c02331edc3a.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"298\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 70\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The Dark Crystal: Age of Resistance is a story revolving around the conflict between two races, Gelfling and Skeksis. You can easily tell which side is good and which side is evil. <br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f628d7357a92af69ccca.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f628d7357a92af69ccca.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"342\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 71\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Game character designers also use shape contrast to denote good and bad characters (like in old animated movies).</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7f7110f50fdc0f92112b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7f7110f50fdc0f92112b.webp\" width=\"1087\" height=\"917\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 72\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Examples from Little Devil Inside.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/83255d097d249fc00e93.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/83255d097d249fc00e93.webp\" width=\"700\" height=\"296\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 73\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d387f7b4a5faeb030147.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d387f7b4a5faeb030147.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"294\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 74\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>The two main characters of the Megaman X series—X and Zero—have contrast not only in colors but also in shapes. The triangular design reflects Zero’s more aggressive and unstable personality.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0e5d8b71426a2c61ef38.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0e5d8b71426a2c61ef38.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"833\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 75\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>In Transformers: Prime, the Autobots have rounder shapes than the Decepticons.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/38d331606b51871c5d45.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/38d331606b51871c5d45.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"304\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 76\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>In Warcraft III, when Arthas was still a Paladin, his design mainly consisted of round and square shapes. But once he became the Lich King, his design got sharper and pointier.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/94a52ac190ea4489212c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/94a52ac190ea4489212c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"777\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 77\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>The humans in World of Warcraft tend to have round designs in contrast with the pointy designs of the non-human characters.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e46c2dafbbe17e00b34b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e46c2dafbbe17e00b34b.webp\" width=\"776\" height=\"438\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 78\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/40180faec4f182dea0f5.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/40180faec4f182dea0f5.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"263\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 79\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The shape contrast in the Darksiders series is similar to that of World of Warcraft.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8dd448b302be97cb6444.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8dd448b302be97cb6444.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"322\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 80\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Beyond geometry</strong></p>\n<p>Sticking to just three basic shapes can be limiting. You can also base your character design on other less common shapes, a teardrop for example.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/71f50ebe733de4d9433b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/71f50ebe733de4d9433b.webp\" width=\"812\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 81\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Megara in Hercules is a combination of jugs and the classic Ionic column.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0e5ba4cceed35268abbd.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0e5ba4cceed35268abbd.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"347\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 82\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>These characters take inspiration from candles.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f45c08034eaa7516cab4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f45c08034eaa7516cab4.webp\" width=\"622\" height=\"882\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 83\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/493aa049e2b63a719732.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/493aa049e2b63a719732.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"387\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 84\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<h2>Chapter 03: Environmental Design</h2>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>TABLE OF CONTENT</strong></p><p><strong>Chapter 03: Environmental Design </strong></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Circle</li><li>Rectangle</li><li>Triangle</li><li>Contrast</li></ul></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>CONTENT</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\n<p>Shapes can dictate the way we perceive an object. Having distinct and consistent shape language within an environment helps establish mood and intention: Is it dangerous or welcoming?</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b7aff16c60f4cefa7c6b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b7aff16c60f4cefa7c6b.webp\" width=\"799\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 85\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circle</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Circular/spherical objects are approachable.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/fb3312dcc4147280325e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/fb3312dcc4147280325e.webp\" width=\"904\" height=\"376\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 86\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e626590e7e3006e69917.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e626590e7e3006e69917.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"347\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 87\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Circular/spherical objects are approachable.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ac1c2ecce5e2e37d3aaf.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ac1c2ecce5e2e37d3aaf.webp\" width=\"501\" height=\"282\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 88\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/086bef0fb4ed509cf11d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/086bef0fb4ed509cf11d.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"322\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 89\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Every element here has a degree of roundness.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e7e4a3088aae15143ce6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e7e4a3088aae15143ce6.webp\" width=\"999\" height=\"451\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 90\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1f19427858401fd7c478.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1f19427858401fd7c478.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"258\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 91\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1b23027599aa82996329.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1b23027599aa82996329.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"455\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 92\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/74256e44196a738f0af0.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/74256e44196a738f0af0.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"429\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 93\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c1220b3ae2b5839dadf7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c1220b3ae2b5839dadf7.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"376\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 94\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/622766ddb6fc1ad94127.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/622766ddb6fc1ad94127.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"494\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 95\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXTRA</strong></p>\n<p>Even though circles are often harmless, you still can roll a giant boulder on people.</p>\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>A giant head also works.</strong></p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d4c3c6c88b87dc68fda3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d4c3c6c88b87dc68fda3.webp\" width=\"809\" height=\"500\" style=\"--source-width:261px\" alt=\"Illustration 96\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></div></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d1515a82b9e9361b3ba3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d1515a82b9e9361b3ba3.webp\" width=\"738\" height=\"877\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 97\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Circular designs also suggest spinning motion (a cog or a wheel). Game developers use this basic knowledge to differentiate a static object (rectangle) from a rotating one (circle).<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c765ed8f6ceefda66deb.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c765ed8f6ceefda66deb.webp\" width=\"498\" height=\"279\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 98\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7b49adce924f714442b0.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7b49adce924f714442b0.webp\" width=\"842\" height=\"473\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 99\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>This artwork is called “Soul Weaver”. There is a handful of circular elements in it: the cogs and the thread spools. They lend a sense of movement to the environment, despite its static nature.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/bf9cfe5e2fc4b6db5736.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/bf9cfe5e2fc4b6db5736.webp\" width=\"1053\" height=\"875\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 100\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Rectangle</strong></p>\n<p>Square or rectangular shapes are sturdy and heavy. These objects feel hard to move or to break. Besides, they also feel manufactured (because most manufactured objects are square).</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e0428f734c03223771ad.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e0428f734c03223771ad.webp\" width=\"857\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 101\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5938fcdac7e2e4bbd77d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5938fcdac7e2e4bbd77d.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"425\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 102\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d29881671cb903c17a39.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d29881671cb903c17a39.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"487\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 103\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9128fa773319e4eef2cd.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9128fa773319e4eef2cd.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"481\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 104\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c944e9efbc48b1d2e0f5.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c944e9efbc48b1d2e0f5.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"501\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 105\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/60434ac09e0500a41307.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/60434ac09e0500a41307.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"570\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 106\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3250efc1a85f5c1d63e1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3250efc1a85f5c1d63e1.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"434\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 107\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c39788c1542e0d367cb7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c39788c1542e0d367cb7.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"442\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 108\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/12751a0a1eef75a9ce72.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/12751a0a1eef75a9ce72.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"568\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 109\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7b7a0bf7d1216ff21551.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7b7a0bf7d1216ff21551.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"561\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 110\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Rectangle shapes permeate The Last of Us 2 as the game takes place in abandoned cityscapes. The use of rectangles also serves as covers for both stealth and gunfight.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/61abfd0e958b21b83817.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/61abfd0e958b21b83817.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"385\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 111\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Control takes place entirely in a Brutalist skyscraper. Thus, there are a lot of blocky shapes.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c2ff64e73feb4fd3dbc0.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c2ff64e73feb4fd3dbc0.webp\" width=\"775\" height=\"438\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 112\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/75467c24099564906006.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/75467c24099564906006.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"264\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 113\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Control takes place entirely in a Brutalist skyscraper. Thus, there are a lot of blocky shapes.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/beae34ea283e308aef46.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/beae34ea283e308aef46.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"323\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 114\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/cc2719db51603705cce6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/cc2719db51603705cce6.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"323\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 115\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f250cc2433b5934f76cf.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f250cc2433b5934f76cf.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"325\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 116\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4afc01b7dce44da4ccbf.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4afc01b7dce44da4ccbf.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"323\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 117\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXTRA—</strong>Gameplay applications</p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Game designers often use rectangular objects for covers.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c0b1fffcee06297bdf56.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c0b1fffcee06297bdf56.webp\" width=\"421\" height=\"238\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 118\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d17eea17b860e4797337.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d17eea17b860e4797337.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"307\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 119\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>They also use rectangular objects for navigational tools.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/df8e11df20e89b9a5f53.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/df8e11df20e89b9a5f53.webp\" width=\"791\" height=\"881\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 120\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Triangle</strong></p>\n<p>We often see triangles in sharp objects such as spikes, swords, spears, arrows, etc. They are all physically harmful. Similarly, an environment filled with spiky shapes will evoke an uneasy feeling.</p>\n<p>For example, people feel comfortable walking into a lush forest, but they will feel nervous walking into a dead one. You can sharpen certain elements in a scene to make it feel more dangerous. But  you need to make sure everything fits within the context.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/25176984031174bc85f9.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/25176984031174bc85f9.webp\" width=\"787\" height=\"936\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 121\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>You can compare these two pictures to better understand our previous point. These two castles both reside in icy mountain ranges. But the bottom one feels more treacherous due to its repeated spiky shapes.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3d10fcfdc77328665d7a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3d10fcfdc77328665d7a.webp\" width=\"854\" height=\"869\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 122\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Similarly, the castle in the left picture looks less threatening than the one in the right due to shape differences. <a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0629b61a7fb95bd3174c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0629b61a7fb95bd3174c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"320\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 123\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Likewise, a dead forest with spiky shapes is inherently more threatening than a lush one.</p>\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p>Just by making the shapes less sharp, the scene became more welcoming</p><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/012e81607e7f5d219a81.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/012e81607e7f5d219a81.webp\" width=\"789\" height=\"457\" style=\"--source-width:261px\" alt=\"Illustration 124\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></div></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/67c6f61e471635678084.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/67c6f61e471635678084.webp\" width=\"789\" height=\"910\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 125\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The dead forests from Beauty and The Beast and The Jungle Book.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/366f13c12158eec480ca.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/366f13c12158eec480ca.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"325\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 126\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>When Snow White ran away from the hunter, the animators used sharp edges in the environment to visualize her fear.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d59b586e4512fa6095ab.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d59b586e4512fa6095ab.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"429\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 127\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d6d001f8746fed1fd774.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d6d001f8746fed1fd774.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"286\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 128\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Similarly, Mulan has a scene with a burnt down town, full of triangular shapes.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/db416d69abc082029ea3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/db416d69abc082029ea3.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"685\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 129\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>These pictures come from the early footage of Black Myth: Wukong. As you can see the spiky shapes of the wooden boardwalk make the scene more intimidating than the lush forest.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3b705aca544965b62234.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3b705aca544965b62234.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"323\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 130\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>The green landscape in Klaus has a lot of curvy lines and circular shapes while the village has a lot of edges and triangular shapes. It makes one place more welcoming, the other more threatening.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/bac0978d24d341fcff1e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/bac0978d24d341fcff1e.webp\" width=\"923\" height=\"907\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 131\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>We can also apply this technique to rock formation to make one environment more treacherous than the other.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/35ee0ed09c262a6a103b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/35ee0ed09c262a6a103b.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"308\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 132\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>More triangular rock formations.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3dafb4c9747eaafebd1c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3dafb4c9747eaafebd1c.webp\" width=\"689\" height=\"353\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 133\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e5eeb6624648e3279be6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e5eeb6624648e3279be6.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"314\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 134\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Death Stranding populates its world with spiky rocks to make traversal more challenging.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/bbafa12692831b338728.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/bbafa12692831b338728.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"434\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 135\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>These abandoned environments in TLOU2 incorporate sharp, pointy elements to evoke danger. <br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7a10e5a89bfd6b0524d7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7a10e5a89bfd6b0524d7.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"501\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 136\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The glass fragments make the scene feel more dangerous and harmful.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/421d0de1b5db02f04571.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/421d0de1b5db02f04571.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"322\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 137\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e83f2686bfdaba920d6b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e83f2686bfdaba920d6b.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"509\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 138\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/6a223969831f25db2a57.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/6a223969831f25db2a57.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"526\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 139\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Contrast</strong></p>\n<p>We can use contrasting shapes (along with other art elements) to create a focal point.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1e35cf39d11bb6b6f858.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1e35cf39d11bb6b6f858.webp\" width=\"942\" height=\"941\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 140\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<p>The ring in each picture stands out because they are the biggest circular shape in their respective composition.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0e345ca1383f5ca8fdfc.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0e345ca1383f5ca8fdfc.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"365\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 141\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/52c3484d705b42430619.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/52c3484d705b42430619.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"479\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 142\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/30487ecfa11f178f1bdd.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/30487ecfa11f178f1bdd.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"532\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 143\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>We can also use shape contrast to attract players’ attention.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f0c007180cb7115332c2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f0c007180cb7115332c2.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"260\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 144\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>These pictures are converted to grayscale to help you focus on the shape contrasts better.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/118fb4d3271158e69884.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/118fb4d3271158e69884.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"719\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 145\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<h2>Chapter 04: Composition</h2>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>TABLE OF CONTENT</strong></p><p><strong>Chapter 04: Composition </strong></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Circle</li><li>Triangle</li><li>A frame within a frame</li></ul></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>CONTENT</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\n<p>Shapes can help us compose a scene. In this section, we will touch upon different compositional techniques using the primary shapes.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8279968af3b3aefc3889.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8279968af3b3aefc3889.webp\" width=\"985\" height=\"940\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 146\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circle</strong></p>\n<p>Circles move our eyes around the composition.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e832878b131c374eadce.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e832878b131c374eadce.webp\" width=\"792\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 147\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE—Circular composition</strong></p>\n<p>The radial composition allows viewers to explore every detail around the central point.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5e8f4a6c556fd56d805c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5e8f4a6c556fd56d805c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"478\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 148\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>By repeating the bridge multiple times, the artist leads our eyes around the picture.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/19ca537580e9d99d122f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/19ca537580e9d99d122f.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"323\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 149\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The weapons and armor create a continuous sense of movement, leading us across the artwork.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/414228c7786c00703289.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/414228c7786c00703289.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"491\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 150\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The spiral moves our attention across the picture, as if we are on the ship.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1e55d0d5f5a1b0976f81.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1e55d0d5f5a1b0976f81.webp\" width=\"808\" height=\"345\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 151\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The curves in these artworks not only lead our eyes around the compositions but also create an illusion of motion.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9c7dc18b7e22b554b126.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9c7dc18b7e22b554b126.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"426\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 152\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3b22010ef16fd4166e77.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3b22010ef16fd4166e77.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"649\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 153\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d12f249ddd6c324381ef.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d12f249ddd6c324381ef.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"482\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 154\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b18617efff6647fdc4ee.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b18617efff6647fdc4ee.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"491\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 155\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Triangle</strong></p>\n<p>In composition, triangles often act as an arrow guiding the viewers’ attention to a particular subject within a frame.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5ab5418e9523bc793fec.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5ab5418e9523bc793fec.webp\" width=\"940\" height=\"925\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 156\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p>An upward triangle also suggests power as it points to someone at the very top (having control over everything below).</p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/de25a84e3da2682728e1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/de25a84e3da2682728e1.webp\" width=\"963\" height=\"546\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 157\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></td><td><p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9bf7295118da64217aac.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9bf7295118da64217aac.webp\" width=\"874\" height=\"881\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 158\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>We can also use negative space to create a downward triangle that leads the eye to the ground.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e3bee212e140e418c295.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e3bee212e140e418c295.webp\" width=\"726\" height=\"321\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 159\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b0852b4e31458e8f42f1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b0852b4e31458e8f42f1.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"320\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 160\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>These two triangles draw our attention across the compositions by going from left to right. But there is still one difference:</p>\n<ul><li>In the left picture, the triangle specifically leads our eye to the main character.</li><li>In the right picture, the triangle shows us the direction to which she is heading.</li></ul>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c1b2a367a035b6801e58.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c1b2a367a035b6801e58.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"275\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 161\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>A frame within a frame</strong></p>\n<p>By adding another frame within the frame, we can focus the viewers’ attention on a specific area. Even though rectangular frames are the most common, other shapes still can work similarly.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0b571189b1297c1faec6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0b571189b1297c1faec6.webp\" width=\"809\" height=\"339\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 162\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9843b45145a859ef70d4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9843b45145a859ef70d4.webp\" width=\"513\" height=\"600\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 163\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p>Video games often use this technique in level design to guide players through the environments. Although developers hand the camera to players, they still can control the approach to their level. For instance, existing architectural openings are perfect opportunities for this technique.</p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9f5cd8a50c0025225f44.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9f5cd8a50c0025225f44.webp\" width=\"874\" height=\"478\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 164\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/dc89faf9431dae3a3662.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/dc89faf9431dae3a3662.webp\" width=\"767\" height=\"868\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 165\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXTRA</strong>—frame within a frame in The Last of Us 2</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p>\n<p>The width of the frame also has an emotional impact on viewers. The less space people have around them, the more uncomfortable they feel. Narrow frames evoke mystery and horror.</p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/13d13ce364c469eb276e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/13d13ce364c469eb276e.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"331\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 166\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>P.T, the cancelled Silent Hills game, intentionally used small and repetitive corridors to build tension and claustrophobia.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/eaf549898d759a0526b1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/eaf549898d759a0526b1.webp\" width=\"913\" height=\"515\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 167\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/527b38fcdf904cb74259.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/527b38fcdf904cb74259.webp\" width=\"883\" height=\"883\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 168\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>You can also frame with triangles.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4c1d82033fd01dbe37c2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4c1d82033fd01dbe37c2.webp\" width=\"1028\" height=\"433\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 169\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d005f7dfc7dba8625b47.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d005f7dfc7dba8625b47.webp\" width=\"767\" height=\"879\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 170\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>We can use openings in natural environment to frame a scene just as effectively.<br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8f7a945b4dd6cc2985a3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8f7a945b4dd6cc2985a3.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"322\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 171\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/befee6d0e0905f725c3b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/befee6d0e0905f725c3b.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"328\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 172\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>The gap between the buildings frames the ground, and the light on the street frames the characters.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3e230dc40e0cd708944d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3e230dc40e0cd708944d.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"325\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 173\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/eb4e6b0807554597a6b0.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/eb4e6b0807554597a6b0.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"535\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 174\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXTRA</strong>—Blocking</p>\n<p>In cinema, blocking refers to the way the director stage his actors to tell a story, as well as leading the audience’s eyes to a focal point.</p>\n<p>Shapes and lines are two common elements of blocking a scene.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/58d5151c6bf24022cab8.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/58d5151c6bf24022cab8.webp\" width=\"884\" height=\"883\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 175\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>A frame full of circles creates a sense of wholeness, unification, or simply friendliness.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4c8f8ef3336198c9a9c1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4c8f8ef3336198c9a9c1.webp\" width=\"793\" height=\"415\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 176\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3b6e45cb821e0f221e04.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3b6e45cb821e0f221e04.webp\" width=\"942\" height=\"883\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 177\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Putting people in a rectangle suggests that they are on an equal footing—literally or figuratively. They could be doing or experiencing something similar together.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/56c14a019c7ff968642f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/56c14a019c7ff968642f.webp\" width=\"829\" height=\"351\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 178\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/61559200a3a32324fa1b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/61559200a3a32324fa1b.webp\" width=\"1005\" height=\"884\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 179\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Triangles can point people to the main subject.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ac16e7aeed051f4cc41e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ac16e7aeed051f4cc41e.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"330\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 180\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>If you have three or more people within a frame, you can put them in a triangular composition to depict their conflict.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/26520f132b7d863fc56f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/26520f132b7d863fc56f.webp\" width=\"793\" height=\"447\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 181\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3ef068bda2851a581e2d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3ef068bda2851a581e2d.webp\" width=\"1007\" height=\"868\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 182\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Sanjuro (1962): in this shot, the group is staged in a box (they are together and equal), but their eyesight leads us to the protagonist, forming a triangle.</p>\n<p>Just from the blocking, we can tell who is who and what they are thinking.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ec28bdafe4aa90b1ac71.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ec28bdafe4aa90b1ac71.webp\" width=\"859\" height=\"868\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 183\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>God of War (2018): during this moment, Kratos and Freya were discussing about Atreus; even though the child was outside, he was still a part of the conversation—similar to the childhood flashback in Citizen Kane.<br></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e5507915f6831deb0cf9.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e5507915f6831deb0cf9.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"368\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 184\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><strong>The Bad Sleep Well (1960) — The Geometry of a Scene</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<h2>Chapter 05: VFX</h2>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>TABLE OF CONTENT</strong></p><p><strong>Chapter 05: VFX </strong></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Circle</li><li>Rectangle</li><li>Triangle</li><li>Closing words</li></ul></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>CONTENT</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\n<p>VFX convey an idea to players. If something is circling them, it should protect them. If something is pointing at them, it may hurt them. So on and so forth. Thus, a consistent shape language helps people understand what a special effect does.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8726b36bfc627663b549.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8726b36bfc627663b549.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"650\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 185\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/eca77e309052cfd23707.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/eca77e309052cfd23707.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"651\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 186\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circle</strong></p>\n<p>In VFX, circles can represent a number of things: a fireball, a shield, a portal, an explosion, etc.</p>\n<p>Rectangles and triangles do appear but less common.</p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5c3f49677accaf5ace17.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5c3f49677accaf5ace17.webp\" width=\"832\" height=\"468\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 187\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0b76a47fbb90f9ab9d2e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0b76a47fbb90f9ab9d2e.webp\" width=\"361\" height=\"444\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 188\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong>—<strong>Circles as shields</strong></p>\n<p>A magical shield can function like a physical shield, meaning it can block from one direction.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c7f9076a27fe16763e0c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c7f9076a27fe16763e0c.webp\" width=\"783\" height=\"325\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 189\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b284ba7b4cc716df6e79.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b284ba7b4cc716df6e79.webp\" width=\"480\" height=\"338\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 190\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Spherical shields, on the other hand, protect the user from all directions.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a0515edfb279df9701d6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a0515edfb279df9701d6.webp\" width=\"480\" height=\"334\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 191\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ffc749a864b56b9fab60.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ffc749a864b56b9fab60.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"325\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 192\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circles as time magic</strong></p>\n<p>As we said in the beginning, circles also represent time (like a clock). Thus, video games often use the clockwork for time magic.</p></td><td><p>Stop magic in<em> Final Fantasy VII</em> Remake</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/984f303a3d91b1f6a42d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/984f303a3d91b1f6a42d.webp\" width=\"764\" height=\"431\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 193\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/67f87b1575062711846f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/67f87b1575062711846f.webp\" width=\"914\" height=\"543\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 194\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circles as magical time shields</strong></p>\n<p>By combining the previous two characteristics—protection &amp; time, we can create a bubble that slows down or outright stops time.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7dff54b66dc2ada7517f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7dff54b66dc2ada7517f.webp\" width=\"600\" height=\"338\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 195\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4f652ddd6ddabfc60160.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4f652ddd6ddabfc60160.webp\" width=\"473\" height=\"301\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 196\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circles as motion</strong></p>\n<p>Circles also remind people of spinning movements (from a wheel or a fan).</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/91b9eb9ef54a5465a519.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/91b9eb9ef54a5465a519.webp\" width=\"864\" height=\"479\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 197\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4f23139d624b2bec2a9f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4f23139d624b2bec2a9f.webp\" width=\"777\" height=\"892\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 198\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Circles as portals</strong></p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Circles are also holes. They can act as a tube that lead us from one place to another.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/64cee02a3354e704b5ff.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/64cee02a3354e704b5ff.webp\" width=\"924\" height=\"466\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 199\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/66898e3e5c7d5c8cd555.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/66898e3e5c7d5c8cd555.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"238\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 200\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Rectangle</strong></p>\n<p>Due to its sturdy nature, rectangles are suitable for blockers, and even shields sometimes.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/656681d28a7ccfee2a1a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/656681d28a7ccfee2a1a.webp\" width=\"774\" height=\"937\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 201\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong>—Rectangle</p>\n<p>Video games have different ways of using walls. Some walls will block people, some block projectiles, other damage who come into contact. One thing that sets rectangular and circular shields apart is their size. Rectangular ones are often bigger, thus can cover more people.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/6b447f225fce6fe12b7f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/6b447f225fce6fe12b7f.webp\" width=\"872\" height=\"484\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 202\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/ca8cd07ce7ecd277bd1d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/ca8cd07ce7ecd277bd1d.webp\" width=\"777\" height=\"884\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 203\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Triangle</strong></p>\n<p>VFX artists often use triangles for high-damage abilities. Sometimes, they are used in tandem with other shapes to improve clarity.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/593a770752c4195700d7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/593a770752c4195700d7.webp\" width=\"831\" height=\"592\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 204\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7371bafb54741ba10381.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7371bafb54741ba10381.webp\" width=\"1000\" height=\"400\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 205\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong>—TRIANGLE</p>\n<div class=\"source-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><p>In the game, triangles represent projectiles that deal heavy damage.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/da80c46bb29afd434594.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/da80c46bb29afd434594.webp\" width=\"552\" height=\"265\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 206\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e5a7a73b4fff4fd28e53.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e5a7a73b4fff4fd28e53.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"294\" style=\"--source-width:130px\" alt=\"Illustration 207\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Ice-damaging spells often have spiky shapes.<br><br><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/dc3edbdf465700790ccf.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/dc3edbdf465700790ccf.webp\" width=\"649\" height=\"366\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 208\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1e6ac3e9e4fc16d4e4f6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1e6ac3e9e4fc16d4e4f6.webp\" width=\"425\" height=\"566\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 209\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Lightning Spear is a spell in Diablo 4 that sends a heat-seeking electric arrow.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/eacd1a927c9e9decac53.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/eacd1a927c9e9decac53.webp\" width=\"951\" height=\"541\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 210\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p>Rupture in the game unleashes spikes from the ground.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f053dc205b19f1fb90cc.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f053dc205b19f1fb90cc.webp\" width=\"851\" height=\"396\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 211\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>This is the Fissure ability in Dota 2. It blocks the pathway and damage enemies. It is a rectangular wall with triangular pieces.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5d15bcf7b83043ecb582.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5d15bcf7b83043ecb582.webp\" width=\"556\" height=\"566\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 212\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>In <em>Final Fantasy VII</em> (and its remake), there is a spell that creates a triangular prism to immobilize a target. Even though it forms a barrier around your character, it locks them in place, removing them from the battle temporarily.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/421c433e79e5e67ec64e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/421c433e79e5e67ec64e.webp\" width=\"703\" height=\"884\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 213\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>We can combine circles and spiky shapes to create fireballs.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/db6d7814958b143788d6.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/db6d7814958b143788d6.webp\" width=\"903\" height=\"548\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 214\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2a59c5feb0eacf715f5e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2a59c5feb0eacf715f5e.webp\" width=\"721\" height=\"880\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 215\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>These lightning balls have a circular core and spiky shapes trailing around.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/464c2e787a529a51e65b.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/464c2e787a529a51e65b.webp\" width=\"595\" height=\"336\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 216\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4daf639ad03f39a18d42.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4daf639ad03f39a18d42.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"615\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 217\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>The<strong> Earthquake</strong> ability in Diablo 3 has a circular radius, but there are spiky shapes in addition to convey its damaging quality.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3e312b655a66ec7faed4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3e312b655a66ec7faed4.webp\" width=\"657\" height=\"411\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 218\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td><td><p>The <strong>Aegis Assault</strong> ability in the game combines a round shape and multiple spiky shapes.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/9b3f31cd1f0b165a6d59.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/9b3f31cd1f0b165a6d59.webp\" width=\"1070\" height=\"896\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 219\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>EXTRA</strong>—AURA</p>\n<p>Perhaps the area in which VFX artists have to mix shapes the most is aura. An aura often have a circle as the primary shape, and other shapes are added to communicate the effect clearer.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/57f4d0bbfae947653677.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/57f4d0bbfae947653677.webp\" width=\"720\" height=\"480\" style=\"--source-width:276px\" alt=\"Illustration 220\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><strong>Green</strong> = offensive<br><strong>Blue</strong> = supportive</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b81a8b664145537e82e2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b81a8b664145537e82e2.webp\" width=\"817\" height=\"897\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 221\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Closing words</strong></p>\n<p>Hardly any design is made of one shape; hardly can shape alone make a design. There are other elements that we need to consider such as color and lighting. But shapes do play a big role in conveying a design intention to viewers.</p>\n<p>We hope the fundamentals presented in this document can help you create meaningful artworks—whether you decide to follow or to bend them.</p></td><td><p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/b3dee2df02b3d5b648fb.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/b3dee2df02b3d5b648fb.webp\" width=\"861\" height=\"514\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 222\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p>And keep in mind that there are more shapes than just the primitive trinity<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/7a49ea43c28168ff24f8.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/7a49ea43c28168ff24f8.webp\" width=\"861\" height=\"375\" style=\"--source-width:269px\" alt=\"Illustration 223\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>";
